NAME
    editor - select nano, vim or vi as the available terminal editor

SYNOPSIS
    editor [argument ...]

DESCRIPTION
    editor is a thin terminal-editor wrapper.

    It selects the first available backend in this order:

        nano
        vim
        vi

    All arguments are passed unchanged and in their original order to the
    selected backend.

    editor does not define or reinterpret editor options, resolve file paths,
    inspect terminal state, rewrite backend diagnostics, or normalize backend
    exit statuses.

BACKEND POLICY
    nano
        Preferred whenever available.

    vim
        Used when nano is unavailable.

    vi
        Final fallback when neither nano nor vim is available.

    Selection is based on command availability, not operating-system identity.

ARGUMENTS
    argument
        Argument passed unchanged to the selected backend. Zero or more
        arguments are accepted.

EXIT STATUS
    The exit status is the status of the selected backend, or the shell
    execution-failure status if the selected backend cannot be executed.
    editor does not define a normalized backend-independent status mapping.

